\end{equation}
By definition, $\sum_{j \in \mathcal{S}_t^c} a_{t,j}^{\mathrm{full}} = \delta_t$. So, the first term is bounded by $\delta_t \max_{j \in \mathcal{S}_t^c} \|v_j\|$.

For the second term from Eq.~\ref{eq:appendix_triangle}, since $\delta_t$ is a non-negative scalar:
\begin{equation}
\| \delta_t h_t^{\mathrm{sparse}} \| = \delta_t \| h_t^{\mathrm{sparse}} \|
\end{equation}
Substituting these bounds back into Eq.~\ref{eq:appendix_triangle} gives the final result:
\begin{equation}
\|h_t^{\mathrm{full}} - h_t^{\mathrm{sparse}}\| \leq \delta_t \max_{j \in \mathcal{S}_t^c} \|v_j\| + \delta_t \| y_t^{\mathrm{sparse}} \|
\end{equation}
Factoring out $\delta_t$ completes the proof:
\begin{equation}
\|h_t^{\mathrm{full}} - h_t^{\mathrm{sparse}}\| \leq \delta_t \left( \max_{j \in \mathcal{S}_t^c} \|v_j\| + \|h_t^{\mathrm{sparse}}\| \right)
\end{equation}

